SUMMARY:Woodworking Workshops for Women
DESCRIPTION:Woodworking Workshops for Women\nCome enjoy woodworking in Seb
 astopol. Learn a new skill in our light-filled studio with other women or 
 renew by starting a new project. Or give a class to a friend or loved one.
  Hope to see you soon!\n\nThe two-day class covers in the fundamentals of 
 furniture making\, using time-honored joinery\, taught in a supportive sho
 p environment with a maximum of 12 women. We will begin building a bench t
 hat can be used as seating for up to 2 people or as a small table.\n-Learn
  to use traditional woodworking hand tools\; chisels\, dovetail saws\, ben
 ch and block planes\, drills.\n-Make mortise and tenon joinery with tusk w
 edges and foxtail wedges\n-Develop the skills and understand the process o
 f building furniture with traditional joinery.\nClass fee is $300- plus a 
 $60- materials fee All tools are supplied.\nClass hours are: Saturday\, 10
 am to 5pm and Sunday\, 10am-4pm.\n\nDebey Zito\, a professional furniture 
 maker who has who has been designing\, building and teaching furniture mak
 ing for 50 years\, is the instructor.\nThe focus of the class is learning 
 joinery and developing hand tool skills. You may not finish your bench in 
 one weekend. You can complete it at home or join another class as an ongoi
 ng student.\nOngoing students make a second project of their own design. A
  monthly Saturday and/or Sunday class is available.\nThe studio is in Seba
 stopol\, one hour north of the Golden Gate Bridge.\nExamples of our furnit
 ure can be seen at: Zito Schmitt Design\n\nIf you would like to read more 
 about us:\nSFCurbed ZitoSchmitt Design\nPress Democrat\nSonoma West (If yo
 u click on the magazine to the left you will see the images)\nAnd of cours
 e\, as always check out our Facebook Page\n\nYou MUST PRE-REGISTER for thi
 s class! Email Debey@zitodesign.com.
